cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark methodology, code, or experimental protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "Benchmark26: A Unified Quantum Program Runtime Estimation Benchmark"
abstract: "A rigorous, leakage-safe benchmarking framework for learning-based and analytical quantum program runtime estimators on physical quantum processing units (QPUs). Features group-disjoint evaluation across 3,443 observations and 203 logical-circuit groups spanning Ma-Li, Qonductor, and QPack corpora."
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dung-h/Benchmark26"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum program runtime estimation
  - qpu benchmark
  - machine learning
  - graph neural networks
  - reproducible research
